    <section class="custom" aria-labelledby="how-title">
      <div class="wrap custom-grid">
        <div class="custom-intro">
          <p class="kicker">How we deliver</p>
          <h2 id="how-title">One bounded workflow at a time.</h2>
          <p>We choose one bounded workflow, agree on the tools, limits and review points, and test the implementation with real data before expanding. That way the automation doesn’t stay a demo; it becomes part of everyday production work.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <ol class="pipeline" aria-label="Example of one bounded workflow">
            <li><span>Data</span>Documents, spreadsheets, systems</li>
            <li><span>Agent</span>Finds, combines and drafts</li>
            <li class="human"><span>Human</span>Reviews exceptions and approves</li>
            <li><span>Done</span>Result and a log of what was done</li>
          </ol>
          <div class="custom-cols">
            <div>
              <h3>Good first targets</h3>
              <ul class="ticks">
                <li>Compiling reports from several sources</li>
                <li>Pre-processing requests for quotation and documents</li>
                <li>Background work for customer service</li>
                <li>Recurring compliance documentation</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Decide before building</h3>
              <ol class="steps">
                <li>Which workflow to automate first.</li>
                <li>Where the data comes from and who owns the outcome.</li>
                <li>Where human approval is needed.</li>
                <li>How the benefit is measured: time, quality, throughput or reduced risk.</li>
              </ol>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

